      "pixel": {
        "detail": "plan.default is not compared: Upstream draws two elements where the reader reads one, twice over: AI Elements writes `asChild` and this shadcn build is Base UI, whose equivalent is `render`, so `<Collapsible asChild><Card>` and `<CollapsibleTrigger asChild><Button>` each nest instead of merging — and the second of those is a <button> inside a <button>, which axe reports and is right to. Taking `asChild` at its word is a decision against upstream's own page, and `parity-divergence.json` records the same one slot by slot. Every other AI Elements example gates at zero.",
        "pass": true
      },
      "snapshot": {
        "pass": true
